WEBVTT

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.540
Look, the sky up above has begun to move.
Hora miageta sora ugokidashita yo

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.770
Your astonishment was so dazzling.
Odoroku kimi mabushikute

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:27.830
Should I forgive the lies you told me yesterday
Kinou tsuita uso mo yurusou kana

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:31.070
just because the morning light is so pretty?
Kesa no hikari kirei dakara

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:38.190
The sound of your laughter is always important to me
Kimi no warai goe itsu datte daiji da yo

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:41.840
because it gives me courage.
Yuuki kureru kara saa

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.700
It's not a lie.
Uso ja nai

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.480
It's a beauty really
It's a beauty really

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:49.630
Your voice whenever.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:50.130
It makes me have.
Your voice whenever.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:51.010
It makes me have.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:51.680
Even the silliest things sound dear,
Sasai na koto mo itoshiku hibiku yo

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:58.000
Sasai na koto mo itoshiku hibiku yo
Even the silliest things sound dear,

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.560
if it's your voice I hear.
kimi no koe nara

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.830
You're sad whenever.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.480
It takes you back.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.860
My heart runneth over.
Hamidasu kokoro

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:16.060
Unable to control myself, I set off at a run.
Osaerarenakute hashiri dashita yo

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:19.070
I can forever.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:35.030
Note: "Kita" = North, "Minami" = South
The North-South War Erupts!

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.170
Christmas.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.400
It's already here...

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.010
Oh yeah, Christmas presents!

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:52.140
Mufflers and mittens, 50% off.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.030
They'd look good on Satsuki.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:58.030
That color would fit Nishino.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:02.100
And that pink would be perfect for Toujou.

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:06.310
It seems too good to be true.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.330
Besides, I've got more time than money on my hands.

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:16.900
This is your first job?

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:18.630
Y-Yes.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:22.790
Understand? I'll be training you extensively until you learn the ropes.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:26.550
Manager, could you please help out in the kitchen?

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:31.510
Satsuki-chan, good timing.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.210
We've got a new hire starting today.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.170
Umm...

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.150
It's Manaka.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:40.180
[Employees' Room]

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:42.020
Satsuki-chan, I'll leave the rest to you.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.680
It looks pretty good on you.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:52.210
Y-You think?

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:56.020
Listen, we have to act like we don't know each other.

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:57.090
Like we're strangers?

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:00.590
If we act all friendly with each other, they'll accuse us of slacking off.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.460
They won't schedule us
to work together.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:06.870
And since when did you start working, Satsuki--

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:11.200
You can't call me
by my first name here!

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.120
Satsuki-chan! Could you cover the register?

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.390
Sure!

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.310
Okay?

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:22.560
Order for one fish, one chicken, and two fries coming in!

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:26.890
Manager, is the teriyaki ready?

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:28.990
Just a bit longer.

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:30.030
New guy!

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:30.890
Yes?

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:34.030
We're running short
on onions, hurry up!

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:35.960
Okay.

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:40.080
Welcome. I'll be taking your orders one by one.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.960
Satsuki-chan's here today.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:44.990
Satsuki-chan, would you like to hang out with me sometime?

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:49.650
Would <i>you</i> like our new Cream Cutlet Burger?

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:50.970
Miss?

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:53.310
When I get older, will you marry me?

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.300
Next person in line please.

00:03:57.850 --> 00:03:59.230
One fish and one chicken!

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:03.190
Satsuki must be the
"main attraction" for this store.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:04.600
New guy!

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:07.010
Aren't those onions done yet?!

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:09.230
I-I'm prepping them right now!

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:12.350
Too slow! When you're done with that, serve the food!

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:13.500
Yes sir...

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:23.660
Thank you very much!

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:29.470
Now that those customers are gone,
the lunch rush is over.

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:32.220
That manager is too rough on his employees.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.720
Speaking of which,
where'd everybody go?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.650
They stepped out to take care of something.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.010
They'll be back around 4:00.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:44.300
So until then, we'll be alone.

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:48.220
We've already finished cleaning up...

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:52.160
And we barely get
any off-peak business.

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:54.880
So, what should we do?

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.370
Do? Do what?

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.400
For starters...

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.080
"For starters"?

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:02.430
Let's practice with the cash register.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:07.000
Running the cash register is the first step to being a fully-trained employee.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:07.880
All right.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.020
L-Like this?

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:16.550
No, first you have to push this button.

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:21.270
A soft feeling on my back...

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:23.490
Yes, this button.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.280
So, once more from the beginning.

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:30.060
Satsuki has a nice smell to her.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:34.810
This is bad, I'm seriously
getting aroused.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:39.500
This is wrong. Satsuki's trying her best to train me,

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.250
and <i>this</i> is how I repay her?

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:46.910
Huh?

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:48.920
Junpei?

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:53.620
Huh? What are those two doing?!

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:56.680
To print a receipt, use this button.

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:58.470
Alone together in this store...

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:02.140
Satsuki must also be expecting something to happen.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:07.430
So what's the problem?
I'll just let my desires lead the way.

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:12.780
S-Satsuki!

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:16.370
Wait a second, you!

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:19.680
Don't cling to Junpei!

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:20.540
What?!

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:23.450
Y-Yui, what're you doing here?!

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.310
It doesn't matter.

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:29.710
I was just walking by, and I saw you being deceived by this woman.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:32.580
It has nothing to do with you.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:33.820
Leave us alone.

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:35.260
Yes it does!

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:39.350
Junpei's parents told me to take care of him.

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:44.100
Well, the <i>manager</i> told <i>me</i> to take care of Manaka.

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:47.320
Neither of them said that.

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:51.100
Anyway, I'm going to study here and keep an eye on you.

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:54.820
Let's see, a bacon cheeseburger,

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:57.690
onion rings and an orange juice as a set.

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:00.630
Junpei, you can cover this for me, right?

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:02.950
Wait just a second, Yui.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:04.050
And also...

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:04.770
What?

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:06.990
Your long hair...

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:09.280
What about my hair?

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:13.770
It's really dirty. I seriously think it's unfit for this job.

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:18.710
Sa-Satsuki...

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:23.960
Manaka~... Who the hell is that annoying brat?!

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:26.200
S-She's a, err, umm,

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:29.720
a childhood friend,
kind of like a younger sister.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.240
It seems like she's got the wrong idea.

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:37.270
That's right, she ordered a bacon cheeseburger...

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:40.400
I'll show her something unforgettable.

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:43.450
Hey Sir! Burger

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:44.740
Sorry for the wait.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:47.250
You wanted a bacon
cheeseburger set, correct?

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:49.150
Please, take your time.

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:51.260
Yay! It's finally here.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:53.050
It looks good!

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:00.960
HA ha, you fell for it!

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:04.250
How do you like the
Spiciness X 30 burger bomb!

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:08.640
It's just the thing to scour out that foul mouth of yours.

00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:12.490
Why you...!

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:15.560
Take the wrath of my mustard beam!

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:18.450
Is this your idea of good customer service?!

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:26.000
Those girls...

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:28.690
Let go!

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:30.950
No, you...

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:34.540
What are you two doing?!

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:35.470
Junpei!
Manaka!

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:38.860
Satsuki, change your outfit.

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:41.800
Yui, you're cleaning the floor with me. Got it?

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:49.570
Even my bra got stained yellow.

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:51.970
I guess I'll wash it real quick and dry it out.

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:54.350
I could swear there was a dryer here.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:58.510
Umm...

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:01.990
What do you want? Either come in here,
or get out and shut the door.

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:04.000
I-I'm sorry.

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:06.700
So, what brings you here?

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:10.450
Junpei told me to come and apologize.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:14.450
I'm sorry for doing those awful things to you.

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:18.500
You're pretty honest, aren't you?

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:22.970
I heard from Junpei that you were

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:25.880
just trying to train him on the register.

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:29.500
I suppose I can live with that.

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:30.800
I see.

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:33.350
What is it?

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.030
Ah, I get it.

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:43.600
You must be jealous of my breasts,

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.120
since you barely have any.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:50.410
How are they?
Do you want to touch them?

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:54.590
I-I don't want breasts like that.

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:57.410
When you get older,
they'll just get all saggy.

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:03.400
She definitely wasn't honest at all.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:05.970
Wait, you!

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:11.760
Insane... I will never eat spicy stuff.

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:14.080
Wait!

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:14.760
Stay away!
Wait!

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:16.690
Stay away!

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:17.490
Yui?

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:20.770
Hold it right there!

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:22.840
Junpei, don't look!

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:33.370
Gotta wash my face--!

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:35.220
You moron!

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:39.220
I've never seen Junpei run that fast before.

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:50.090
You got a death wish, dumbass??

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:04.990
A Christmas All Alone

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:13.010
Hey, new guy! Didn't I say two orders of fries?!

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:15.250
Y-Yes, I'm prepping them now.

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:19.260
One fish, one teriyaki to go,
and one nugget!

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:21.800
So, are you getting used to this,
Mr. New Employee?

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:22.740
Yeah.

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:26.200
But it's sort of strange to see someone working part-time during this season.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:30.450
Maybe it's because you want to buy
your girlfriend a Christmas present?

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:32.980
N-No, I...

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:42.300
Kondou-san, it seems like we don't
have any 10 yen coins in stock.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.410
I'm gonna go exchange some money.
Could you cover the register?

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:46.730
Roger that.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:50.330
She didn't hear us?

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:52.130
Thank goodness.

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:54.860
Stop daydreaming and clean off the tables!

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:55.740
Yes sir!

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:01.920
Welcome!

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:05.340
Junpei-kun, you were working here?

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:09.330
N-Nishino, w-why're you here?

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:11.840
Because, I live right around here.

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:14.600
I'm on my way home
from cooking school.

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:17.470
Eh? Is she your girlfriend, Manaka-kun?

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:19.840
H-Hey now, Kondou-san.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.180
Say, Junpei-kun...

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:23.810
When do you get off work?

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:26.320
Can we meet up after that?

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:30.520
Err, umm...

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:34.050
I just made a roll cake at school.

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:35.750
C'mon, taste-test it for me!

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:37.500
Yeah, why don't you?

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:39.900
Manaka-kun, you're
scheduled until 5:00, right?

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:42.690
You've only got five more minutes. Just take off.

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:44.420
O-Okay.

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:50.170
Thank goodness this happened
when Satsuki wasn't here.

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:57.460
And with that,
I'm now in Nishino's room.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:12:59.510
How is it?

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:02.780
Mmm, it's great.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:04.900
It's better than the store-bought kind.

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:06.180
Really?

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:06.920
Yeah.

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:08.060
Do you want some more?

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:08.910
Thank you.

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:16.920
Nishino really is a good cook.

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:17.920
Hmm, what is it?

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:23.810
Nothing. I was just surprised that they even teach cake-baking at cooking school.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:27.180
Wow, today must be my lucky day.

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:29.670
I guess it is.

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:34.300
Ah, should I put on a CD?

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:39.810
What a lovely view...

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:42.670
I wonder if you'd know this song.

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:46.090
It got used in commercials, too.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:52.360
Behind me, relaxing background music.

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:56.860
And in front of me,
one defenseless girl in a miniskirt.

00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:00.250
This tune's famous, don't you know?

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:04.840
This sort of thing is...
you know, "that".

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:08.510
Isn't this the kind of feeling that
leads up to "that" situation?

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:13.670
I really like this piece.

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:16.670
And as usual, <i>I'm</i> the only one who's nervous?

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:19.070
I've wondered...

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:22.360
...has there ever been a time when Nishino was nervous around me?

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:27.570
Did she only bring me here
to have me taste her cake?

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:30.360
Wait...

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:33.890
Where are your parents today?

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:36.190
Hmm? They'll be coming home soon.

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:37.870
Ah, I see.

00:14:38.150 --> 00:14:41.750
Why am I feeling a mix of
disappointment and relief?

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:43.530
But...

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:47.300
I <i>think</i> they said they wouldn't be back until after 10:00.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:50.950
Then it's just us?!

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:55.980
Well, I guess I should be heading on home.

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:56.930
Why?

00:14:57.260 --> 00:15:00.170
B-Because, it's already dark out.

00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:04.060
The roll cake really
was good. Thank you.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:07.890
I don't think Nishino would have those kinds of intentions, but...

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:12.180
But, in an atmosphere like this...

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:13.770
Things might turn bad.

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:15.280
Wait!

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:17.770
Hey, Junpei-kun?

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:20.890
We're still going out, right?

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:24.480
I-I think this mood is probably...

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:26.950
Erm... pretty dangerous.

00:15:27.490 --> 00:15:28.190
It isn't.

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:32.610
B-But, at this rate,

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:36.160
if we get carried away by this atmosphere, then I...

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:39.020
I...

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:42.560
...want to know what'll happen if we get carried away.

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:52.050
No matter what you
want to try, it's okay.

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:55.570
Ni-Nishino...

00:15:56.770 --> 00:16:00.900
For some reason it feels natural to kiss her right now.

00:16:13.810 --> 00:16:16.170
No, on second thought, wait.

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:23.580
I won't wait any longer.

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:29.180
I just realized it.

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:32.670
I don't like that
"waiting for something" feeling.

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:34.880
Nishino...

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:37.880
Going to different high schools

00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:40.770
really was a mistake, wasn't it?

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:42.300
That's right.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:46.890
You didn't contact me at all during the first semester, and I got tired of waiting.

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:48.770
I thought about breaking up.

00:16:49.130 --> 00:16:53.410
With those thoughts in mind, I went to see you while I still thought I liked you.

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:57.240
Because when I'm with you,

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:59.840
I start to get really excited.

00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:07.020
You even went out of your way to run and meet me on my birthday.

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:10.390
And then we ate cake together.

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:16.230
And at that time, I remembered
your pull-up confession, Junpei-kun.

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:18.860
Because it was another exciting event.

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:24.250
I felt like I could go out
with you forever.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:28.360
But something changed, didn't it?

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:33.840
Thinking back on it,

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:37.550
I also wanted to help you make movies.

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:39.780
I wanted to be next to you

00:17:40.170 --> 00:17:44.000
and become engulfed in your dreams.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:48.840
And anyway, isn't it a waste for such a cute girl

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:52.630
to end up waiting for love forever?

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:56.530
That's why...

00:17:58.010 --> 00:17:59.090
This time...

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:01.910
...it's goodbye.

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:07.680
I couldn't even apologize to her.

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:12.790
Nishino wanted to go out with me as equals.

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:17.120
But Nishino had always been a figure I looked up to.

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:23.060
And with that upward gaze, I hurt Nishino by keeping her waiting.

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:30.290
Customer number 156:
One order of fried chicken!

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:32.010
We are sorry to keep you waiting.

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:34.820
We're too short-staffed!

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:37.720
Manager, chicken
two-pack on the double.

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:41.970
New guy, get the chicken out and prep it for cooking, now!

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:42.490
Yes sir!

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:48.920
This place is always hell around Christmastime.

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:50.300
I'm fine.

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:55.460
Most people wouldn't willingly
volunteer to work Christmas Eve.

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:59.420
Don't you have a party, a date,
or maybe plans with a girlfriend?

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.420
I don't have any plans like that.

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:05.370
You don't have anyone to spend your time with?

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:07.160
No, I don't.

00:19:11.570 --> 00:19:12.920
Welcome!

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.610
We're here to harass you!

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:19.550
Why, oh why?

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:23.240
We're on our way back from a club Christmas meeting.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:27.910
We heard that you were working part-time, so we came to see you.

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:32.910
Manaka, you've been working with Satsuki-chan, haven't you?!

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:36.220
I want to see Satsuki-chan in her uniform!

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:38.510
Should I change into
that right now then?

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:45.490
Manaka, since we're such close friends, give us a 50% discount.

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:47.760
I can't do it; I don't have the power.

00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:54.750
All right, let's give the Film Club
our best effort next year!

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:55.970
Yeah!

00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:01.470
Good luck surviving
the rest of your shift.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:04.590
I suppose I can help out for awhile.

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:05.890
It's okay.

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:08.840
Remember: drink sake, don't get drunk by it.

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:12.000
Sensei, we're still underage.

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:14.150
Now now, let's go home.

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:14.870
Bye.

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:18.590
Manaka-kun, I'll see you
again next year.

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:20.110
I see.

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:22.690
Our first year is already over.

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:26.200
Good work, people.

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:28.290
Good work!

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:36.030
In the end, I sort of ended up spending
Christmas with everyone.

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:39.220
This is...

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:40.600
What do you think?

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:43.620
This is our store's special cake,
"Bouchée du Noël".

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:46.610
This is a Christmas cake?

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:48.680
It is a limited-time
Christmas item.

00:20:49.610 --> 00:20:51.230
B-But, this...

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:54.440
Here you go, Junpei-kun.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:57.530
But, Nishino...

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:00.500
She said she only wanted a cake taste-tester.

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:05.050
Nishino must've known it was
a Christmas cake when she baked it.

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:13.370
Maybe Nishino had planned to spend Christmas with me all along.

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:17.210
And for that sake, she called me out.

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:20.980
Excuse me, sir?

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:28.140
Nishino...

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:32.620
I couldn't stop my tears.

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:37.150
I really did like Nishino.

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:41.930
Even though it wouldn't
do me any good...

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:43.880
...I finally realized it.

